surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hard X-ray phase tomography with low-brilliance sources</article-title><source><italic>Physical Review Letters</italic></source><year>2007</year><volume>98</volume><fpage>4</fpage><comment>108105.</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pfeiffer</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Gr&#x000fc;nzweig</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Bunk</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Frei</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Lehmann</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>David</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Neutron phase imaging and tomography</article-title><source><italic>Physical Review Letters</italic></source><year>2006</year><volume>96</volume><issue>21</issue></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Creath</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Wolf</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Phase measurement interferometry techniques</article-title><source><italic>Progress in Optics XXVI</italic></source><year>1988</year><publisher-loc>Amsterdam, The Netherlands</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Elsevier Science</publisher-name><fpage>349</fpage><lpage>393</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Surrel</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Design of algorithms for phase measurements by the use of phase stepping</article-title><source><italic>Applied Optics</italic></source><year>1996</year><volume>35</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>51</fpage><lpage>60</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Patorski</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><source><italic>Handbook of the Moir&#x000e9; Fringe Technique</italic></source><year>1993</year><publisher-loc>Amsterdam, The Netherlands</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Elsevier Science</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="confproc"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Momose</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Yashiro</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Moritake</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Bonse</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Biomedical imaging by Talbot-type X-ray phase tomography</article-title><volume>6318</volume><conf-name>Developments in X-Ray Tomography V</conf-name><conf-date>August 2006</conf-date><conf-loc>San Diego, Calif, USA</conf-loc><fpage>10</fpage><series>Proceedings of SPIE</series></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Winthrop</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name><name><surname>Worthington</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Theory of fresnel images. I. Plane periodic objects in monochromatic light</article-title><source><italic>Journal of the Optical Society of America</italic></source><year>1965</year><volume>55</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>373</fpage><lpage>381</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Patorski</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type